{"version":"6.9","hitCount":2,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"Oxford Cognitive Screen\" AND FIRST_PDATE:[2015-01-01 TO 2015-12-31]","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":3,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"25730165","source":"MED","pmid":"25730165","doi":"10.1037/pas0000082","title":"The Oxford Cognitive Screen (OCS): validation of a stroke-specific short cognitive screening tool.","authorString":"Demeyere N, Riddoch MJ, Slavkova ED, Bickerton WL, Humphreys GW.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Demeyere N","lastName":"Demeyere","firstName":"Nele","initials":"N","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0416-5147"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Cognitive Neuropsychology Centre."}]}},{"fullName":"Riddoch MJ","lastName":"Riddoch","firstName":"M Jane","initials":"MJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Cognitive Neuropsychology Centre."}]}},{"fullName":"Slavkova ED","lastName":"Slavkova","firstName":"Elitsa D","initials":"ED","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Cognitive Neuropsychology Centre."}]}},{"fullName":"Bickerton WL","lastName":"Bickerton","firstName":"Wai-Ling","initials":"WL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Psychology, University of Birmingham."}]}},{"fullName":"Humphreys GW","lastName":"Humphreys","firstName":"Glyn W","initials":"GW","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Cognitive Neuropsychology Centre."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0416-5147"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"27","journalIssueId":2316525,"dateOfPublication":"2015 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2015,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Psychol Assess","title":"Psychological assessment","essn":"1939-134X","issn":"1040-3590","nlmid":"8915253","isoabbreviation":"Psychol Assess"},"printPublicationDate":"2015-09-01"},"pubYear":"2015","pageInfo":"883-894","abstractText":"There is currently no existing freely available short screen for cognitive problems that targets stroke survivors specifically. We have developed a short cognitive screen, the Oxford Cognitive Screen (OCS), to be completed in 15-20 min, designed for use with stroke patients. To maximize inclusion, the test is aphasia- and neglect friendly and covers domains of cognition where deficits frequently occur after stroke, including apraxia and unilateral neglect as well as memory, language, executive function, and number abilities. Domain-specific scores are returned to help direct rehabilitation. This article presents the normative data in a large sample of 140 neurologically healthy participants, a report on incidences of impairments in a sample of 208 acute stroke patients (within 3 weeks of stroke onset), measures of test-retest reliability on an alternate form and convergent and divergent validity. In addition, the full test materials are made freely available for clinical use.","affiliation":"Cognitive Neuropsychology Centre.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Wellcome Trust","acronym":"WT_","grantId":"102566","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Oxford Cognitive Health Clinical Research Facility","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Stroke Association","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Stroke Association","grantId":"TSA2011/02","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institute for Health Research (NIHR)","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aphasia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DI","qualifierName":"diagnosis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PX","qualifierName":"psychology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Memory Disorders","meshQualifier